    "goal": "Report the binary .bed size (MB), per-chromosome .bed size (MB), and number of per-chromosome files for a GWAS genotype dataset.",
    "rationale": "PLINK binary .bed packs 2 bits per sample per variant, so whole-dataset size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome size uses the same rule applied to the largest chromosome's variant count (950,419). The number of per-chromosome files equals the number of chromosomes in the split (22 autosomes + X = 23, or 24 with Y); this is a property of the chromosome set, not a computed value.",
